# Build context exclusions.
#
# Both Dockerfiles build from the repository root, so this file governs what is
# sent to the daemon. Excluding node_modules is the single biggest win — the
# installed tree here is well over a gigabyte with Puppeteer's Chromium and
# Prisma's engines, and it is reinstalled inside the image regardless.

node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build output. Regenerated in the image; copying it in risks a stale artifact
# silently shipping instead of a fresh build.
dist
**/dist
.next
**/.next
.turbo
**/.turbo
*.tsbuildinfo

# Secrets. A .env in the build context becomes a layer in the image, and layers
# are extractable from any registry the image is pushed to.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Version control and CI
.git
.gitignore
.github

# Local tooling
.vscode
.idea
.claude
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# Tests and coverage — not part of a runtime image, and excluding them keeps a
# source-file change from invalidating the dependency layer.
coverage
**/*.spec.ts
**/__testing__

# Documentation and infrastructure. Neither is needed to run the apps, and both
# change often enough to keep busting the cache if included.
docs
infra
README.md
*.md
